{"id": "EUVD-2026-67437", "enisaUuid": "d57a4003-aceb-34cf-b889-36737914e203", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vmwgfx: fix guest_memory_dirty bitfield clobbered as size\n\nTwo sites in vmwgfx_resource.c assign boolean literals to\nres->guest_memory_size, which is an unsigned long allocation-size\nfield; the intended target is the adjacent res->guest_memory_dirty\nbitfield.  After the assignments the field holds 0 or 1 instead of\nthe resource's MOB allocation size:\n\n  - vmw_resource_release()       writes 0 (false), and\n  - vmw_resource_unbind_list()   writes 1 (true).\n\nSubsequent revalidation paths read guest_memory_size when computing\nthe dirty page range (vmw_bo_dirty_transfer_to_res()) and the buffer\nallocation size (vmw_resource_buf_alloc()), producing zero-length\nwalks or wrap-around ranges that read or write past the MOB bitmap.\nThe dirty-tracking intent of the original code (mark the resource as\ndirtied since the last sync) is also lost, since guest_memory_dirty\nis never updated.\n\nRename both assignments to guest_memory_dirty.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:53:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:34", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21bbe38faee4a195d33a93e3908e307807f7745d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d6cbb76fe9cd760351f6b0b20f1bf788eab8fa6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/282f261cb035e5f01a486f76d356b7e9dbfba73f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b2bb16a5b622867140d69925db411ac8ecb3b2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83195b778f2d109a3a4f3ffaba4dce7e4cdb58aa"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80702", "GHSA-736r-87mh-h3gr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03edddc7-fb04-3488-85ad-408ab96a5a7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668b206601c5f5063e03b76784a0d3024fa2b249 <83195b778f2d109a3a4f3ffaba4dce7e4cdb58aa"}, {"id": "1816e60c-cf29-3423-821f-49259a158df3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "1ae7e881-1604-3619-a5c1-7f1ace601200", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "56cdb3cb-91e0-338a-88a6-a05e84c3dc40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "5a83cdbc-49b3-3647-a85f-c394af125a62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668b206601c5f5063e03b76784a0d3024fa2b249 <282f261cb035e5f01a486f76d356b7e9dbfba73f"}, {"id": "67487ef0-096a-3dd9-9a37-f850a68ffad1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "81f714ab-0bd3-303b-8510-da6b845c71ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "a24e7137-b5c8-359b-9ef1-37eab2304fdb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668b206601c5f5063e03b76784a0d3024fa2b249 <9d6cbb76fe9cd760351f6b0b20f1bf788eab8fa6"}, {"id": "a5c033f9-eebd-32a8-bd20-f6f426205571", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668b206601c5f5063e03b76784a0d3024fa2b249 <21bbe38faee4a195d33a93e3908e307807f7745d"}, {"id": "a5d77f1c-4d5f-3b4b-9c15-74de16b84045", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "f5bcc6e2-914f-395b-89d9-7bb6c76ec0e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "f8236cf8-515c-3534-a1ea-21b7f2b65f81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668b206601c5f5063e03b76784a0d3024fa2b249 <3b2bb16a5b622867140d69925db411ac8ecb3b2b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b015390e-a9a0-3c7f-9b41-1c85f579edd3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}